# ENTERING A UNIT DEMANDS ONLY THE TYPES THAT IMPLEMENT SOMETHING: entryunit's
# `Cfg` holds `limit: page_size`, a bare name, which the unit's one-time entry
# read as an implementation, so it resolved `Cfg` -- and reported its field's
# unknown type -- though nothing here reads it. Only `.implement` declares an
# implementation now, and an unused `Cfg` is only parsed.
main: function is {
    print "\{entryunit.answer}"
}
